Phil,

Provided you can connect up a monitor to the computer with the right type of
connector (SVGA, BNC, 13W3 or other), just about any MULTISYNCHRONOUS monitor
made for PCs or Macs ought to work.  The key is multi-sync, the capability to
synchronize with any frequency of signal within a given range.  There are also
somewhat inexpensive converter cables to handle mismatches between monitor and
computer connectors... Ben Myers

