> I have a Compaq ES40 Alphaserver which has failed to restart following
> a power cycle. The status line on the front of the case is displaying
> 'TIG error' and there is no monitor output.

  We had the exact same situation you described, and CPQ came and
  replaced the mainboard, *BUT* it may not be necessary. We had a
  TIG error because the Flash RAM from wich the TIG loads it's
  code went bye-bye, and altough there is also a ROM with the
  same contents on the mainboard, a jumper controlls what the
  try-sequence is: flash-then-rom or flash-only.

  The factory default setting for the jumper is flash-only.

  I don't know what jumper it was that needed to be switched
  - maybe it's the same someone mentioned abowe -, but the
  info can be found in the ES40 Service Manual wich can be
  downloaded from the web if I recall correctly.

  Hope this helps.

  Oh, btw. the TIG is a microcontroller that initializes the
  whole mainboard with everything on it, so it's not 100%
  sure, that this is the problem but it's worth a try.

