Some time in the past, in a posting that has vanished with time,
the question was raised "what are those two tiny DIP switches in a
Storageworks SBB that holds an SCA disk drive?"

Curiosity finally got the better of me, and I disassembled one to look
carefully.  Switch 1 seems to go to pin 38 of the SCA connector, and
switch 2 to pin 78.  These are RMT_START and DLYD_START respectively.
Meaning "wait for Start Unit command from host", and "delay motor
start by 10 seconds * SCSI ID number".

The switches were set to (on, off) which corresponds to the standard
DEC configuration -- SCSI drives wait for Start Unit from host.

I was hoping that maybe the switches would control something that
would allow using a 16-bit (wide) SBB in an 8-bit (narrow) backplane.
No such luck.

    carl
