I accept your challenge.

A bit of a squeeze, but it fits.

I had to use a "low profile" power extender cable to get the power over
to the other side, because my adapter had the power connector in the
wrong place, but there is enough flexibility in the circuit that I was
able to close the lid on an SBB with the adapter and a narrow Barracuda
standing in for the SCA drive. I don't have a spare SCA drive, but the
'cuda is a plenty big drive and since the SCA connector wasn't plugged
in it took more room than it would with a real SCA drive.

It'd be better with a better designed adapter with the power and SCSI
connection inline in the right order.

The only concern I'd have would be cooling, and since the adapter is no
bigger than the end of a 3.5" HH drive it shouldn't block any more air
than an actual HH drive.

I wouldn't recommend this kind of kludge if you have an alternative, but
if all else fails it should work.

